# Lab 8: NSEC walk. This zone is signed with plain DNSSEC NSEC: every
# answer that says a name does not exist also names the next name that does,
# so anyone can list the whole zone one query at a time. Transfers are
# refused, and two hosts are names no wordlist holds. Run:
#   subenum -simulate-zone lab8 -nsec-walk -format jsonl lab.example
# Then change $DNSSEC to nsec3 in a copy of this file and run it again.
$DNSSEC nsec
@                 A      192.0.2.1
@                 NS     ns1
ns1               A      192.0.2.53
www               A      192.0.2.10
mail              A      192.0.2.20
vpn               A      192.0.2.30
payroll-archive   A      192.0.2.80
qa.build-farm     A      10.30.0.12
